title: Gameplay and UI field editors
intro: The gameplay, UI, story, wiring, data and multiplayer components' fields that took something typed from memory have editors of their own now: formats with holes, lists of names, items and their uses, dialogue flags and choices, and UI areas.
project: Empty | Field Kit Two

chapter: Text with holes | A counter's format
create: Text
rename: Score
add: Counter
explain: field:Counter.Format | Format | A counter's format has holes the game fills in. Each one has a button now, saying what it puts in, and underneath it says how the text reads right now.
click: editor:Counter.Format:insert:{1}
expectvalue: Score.Counter.Format = Score: {0}{1}
explain: editor:Counter.Format:preview | Reads now | The best goes in after the count, and the line under it shows how it reads.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectvalue: Score.Counter.Format = Score: {0}

chapter: Names in order | Sides, and a side picked
create: Turn Order
explain: field:TurnOrder.Sides | Sides | A turn order's sides were names typed with commas between them. Each is a row now, to rename, move up or take out.
click: editor:TurnOrder.Sides:add
editorset: TurnOrder.Sides:name:3 = Pirates
expectvalue: Turns.TurnOrder.Sides = Player, Enemy, Pirates
create: Empty
rename: Captain
add: Turn Taker
pick: TurnTaker.Side = Pirates
expectvalue: Captain.TurnTaker.Side = Pirates
expectflagged: TurnTaker.Side = none
explain: field:TurnTaker.Side | Side | A turn taker's side is picked from the sides there are, and flagged when it names none.

chapter: Items and what they do | An inventory
add: Inventory
explain: field:Inventory.Items | Items | What an inventory holds is a row an item now, with how many.
set: Inventory.Items = Key
editorset: Inventory.Items:count:1 = 3
expectvalue: Captain.Inventory.Items = Key 3
set: Inventory.Item Uses = Potion: heal 3
explain: field:Inventory.Item Uses | Item Uses | And what each item does is a row too: heal, spawn a prefab, or send a message, each picked rather than spelled out.
choose: Inventory.Item Uses:verb:1:1 = send
editorset: Inventory.Item Uses:argument:1:1 = Drank
expectvalue: Captain.Inventory.ItemUses = Potion: send Drank

chapter: A dialogue's flags and choices | The Dialogue Editor
create: Empty
rename: Guide
add: Dialogue
explain: editor:Dialogue.Lines:dialogueeditor | Dialogue Editor | A dialogue's lines say how many lines, choices and parts they hold, with the Dialogue Editor a click away.
click: editor:Dialogue.Lines:dialogueeditor
dialogue
dialogueline: 1
dialogueset: tagkind = set
dialogueset: tagname = MetGuide
click: dialogue:addtag
expectvalue: Guide.Dialogue.Lines = [set MetGuide] Hello!
explain: dialogue:tags | Flags and messages | The flags a line needs, sets and clears, and the messages it sends, are listed in words and added from lists of what the project has.
click: dialogue:addchoice
dialogueset: goesto = End
expectvalue: Guide.Dialogue.Lines = [set MetGuide] Hello!\n> ... -> End
explain: dialogue:goesto | Goes to | And where a choice goes is picked from the dialogue's parts.
click: dialogue:close

chapter: UI areas | Resized in the Scene view
create: Slider
menu: View > Resize Handles
explain: scene | Resize handles | With resize handles out, a slider's size, a button's clickable area or a save slot's picture has handles of its own to drag.
resize: Ctrl+Slider.right = 6
expectvalue: Slider.Slider.Size.X = 6
say: Every one of these is an undo step, and agents get the same choices through the editor's tools.
